%% Diagram 3 - API request/response flow (STUDENT PROTOTYPE).
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as User (browser)
    participant FE as Frontend (script.js)
    participant GW as API Gateway HTTP API
    participant LH as Lambda handler (Mangum)
    participant API as FastAPI app
    participant VAL as Pydantic validation
    participant SVC as Recommendation service
    participant REPO as JSON repository
    participant CW as CloudWatch Logs

    Note over User,CW: Student prototype. All profile data is synthetic.
    User->>FE: Fill profile, click "Generate recommendations"
    FE->>FE: Client-side checks (friendly messages only)
    FE->>GW: POST /recommendations (JSON)
    GW->>LH: Invoke (payload format 2.0)
    Note right of LH: Cold start: module Init loads app + dataset once<br/>Warm: environment reused
    LH->>API: ASGI request (aws.context → request_id)
    API->>VAL: Validate body
    alt Body missing / not JSON / not an object
        VAL-->>API: body-level error
        API-->>FE: 400 {status:"error", error:{code:"INVALID_JSON"...}}
    else Field rule broken (age 12, min>max, duplicate interests...)
        VAL-->>API: field errors
        API-->>FE: 422 {status:"error", error:{code:"VALIDATION_ERROR", details:[...]}}
    else Valid
        API->>REPO: list_candidates() (cached after first call)
        REPO-->>API: 64 synthetic profiles
        API->>SVC: recommend(request, candidates)
        SVC-->>API: ranked top N + reasons + score breakdown
        API-->>LH: 200 JSON + X-Request-ID, X-Response-Time-Ms
        LH-->>GW: HTTP response
        GW-->>FE: 200 {status:"success", recommendations:[...]}
    end
    LH-)CW: {"event":"lambda_invocation","first_invocation_in_env":...}
    FE->>User: Cards with score, reasons, round-trip and server time
